+[Term]
+id: MONDO:7770012
+name: SYCE1-related gametogenic failure
+def: "Any infertility disorder in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the SYCE1 gene, which encodes a central element protein of the synaptonemal complex required for meiotic chromosome synapsis. This condition presents with varying phenotypes depending on chromosomal sex: in 46,XX individuals with primary ovarian insufficiency characterized by premature depletion or dysfunction of oocytes; and in 46,XY individuals with non-obstructive azoospermia due to meiotic failure and maturation arrest." [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/, PMID:31916078, PMID:32402064]
+synonym: "SYCE1 gametogenic failure" EXACT [PMID:31916078, PMID:32402064]
